ent-ClothingNeckBrokenMedal = Broken medal
    .desc = It has been burned so badly that its type can no longer be identified.
ent-ClothingNeckChocoMedal = Chocolate medal
    .desc = Awarded by a mother to the best dishwasher.
ent-ClothingNeckHydraMedal = Hydra Order
    .desc = Awarded to those who leave only ash and death in their wake.
ent-ClothingNeckPlasticMedal = Plastic medal
    .desc = A souvenir medal from Happy Honk toy packs.
ent-ClothingNeckPlasticSpecialMedal = Suspicious plastic medal
    .desc = It looks like a souvenir medal from Happy Honk toy packs, but the clown's eyes shine an unusual red. An inscription on the back reads, "To the best agent, honk."
ent-ClothingNeckPolarIIIMedal = Order of the Polar Star, Third Class
    .desc = A prestigious USSP naval award made of silver and set with star-shaped aquamarine. The green ribbon represents Earth, the green planet.
ent-ClothingNeckPolarIIMedal = Order of the Polar Star, Second Class
    .desc = A prestigious USSP naval award made of gold and silver, with a star-shaped aquamarine inlay. The green ribbon represents Earth, and the blue stripes represent its oceans.
ent-ClothingNeckPolarIMedal = Order of the Polar Star, First Class
    .desc = The highest class of a prestigious USSP naval award. Made of gold and silver, set with aquamarine and the purest sapphires. The green ribbon represents Earth; the blue stripes represent its oceans. It is further decorated with a golden symbol of Earth.
ent-ClothingNeckSSSPMedal = Red Star Medal
    .desc = Awarded for bravery and faithful service in the USSP Red Army.
ent-ClothingNeckSyndieMedal = Syndicate medal
    .desc = That's an award for winning an attraction at SyndiLand, right?
